FEEZIQ PRIVACY POLICY

Last updated: 5 September 2026
Effective: 5 September 2026

Applies to: the Feeziq mobile app for iOS and Android (bundle ID
com.chatrsimab.feeziq), the Feeziq Wear OS / watch companion, and the
website at feeziq.com.


1. WHO WE ARE

Feeziq ("Feeziq", "we", "us") is a health and fitness app operated by
Farzad Chatrsimab, who is the data controller for the personal data
described in this policy.

You can reach us about anything in this policy through feeziq.com.

If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom and
believe we have mishandled your data, you may contact us first and, if
you are not satisfied, lodge a complaint with your national supervisory
authority.


2. THE SHORT VERSION

- Feeziq requires an account. You cannot use the app anonymously.
- We collect the health and fitness information you enter: weight,
  workouts, meals, hydration, goals and body metrics. That is the
  product. Under EU and UK law this is special-category health data, and
  we process it only with your explicit consent, which you give when you
  create an account and can withdraw at any time.
- We do not sell your personal data, and we do not share your health
  data with advertisers.
- Parts of your profile are public to other Feeziq users by design:
  username, display name, photo, biography, sports, XP, streaks,
  achievements and leaderboard standing.
- AI features send your input (a meal photo, a text description, your
  fitness profile) to Google's Vertex AI. Google processes it as our
  service provider and, under our Google Cloud terms, does not use it to
  train its models.
- Free accounts see Google AdMob ads. Ad SDKs collect device and
  advertising identifiers. They do not receive your health data.
- You can delete your account and its data at any time at feeziq.com.


3. WHAT WE COLLECT

3.1 Account and identity

- Email address, from you or from your Google or Apple sign-in, used for
  authentication, account recovery and service notices.
- Password, hashed. Firebase Authentication handles this and we never
  see your password in readable form.
- Google or Apple account identifier, used for authentication. If you
  use Apple's Hide My Email, we only ever hold the relay address.
- A user ID we generate, which ties your records together.
- Display name, username, profile photo and biography, which form your
  public profile.
- Your referral code and who invited you, used for referral rewards.

3.2 Health and fitness data (special category)

- Date of birth and the age derived from it, gender, height
- Weight entries and weight history
- Physical activity level, fitness goal, and the sports you practise
- Dietary triggers, allergies and restrictions you record
- Workouts created, scheduled and completed, including per-set and
  per-exercise detail
- Diet plans, meals logged, portion sizes and nutrition totals
- Hydration entries
- Free-text activity descriptions you write for AI recognition
- Streaks, XP, progress records and achievements

We process this only on the basis of your explicit consent under GDPR
Article 9(2)(a). Withdrawing that consent means deleting your account,
because the app cannot function without this data.

3.3 Content you create

- Direct messages you send to other users. Message content is encrypted
  with AES before it is written to our database and to your device. This
  is encryption at rest, not end-to-end encryption: the key is managed
  by the app, so we retain the technical ability to decrypt messages. We
  do so only where required by law or to investigate abuse reported to
  us.
- Photos you upload: profile picture, workout banners and diet banners.
  These are stored in Firebase Storage.
- Meal photos you scan with the AI meal scanner. These are read from
  your device and sent to Google's Vertex AI for analysis. They are not
  uploaded to our storage and we do not keep them. Only the nutrition
  estimates you choose to save are stored.
- AI Coach conversations, including the profile summary we attach so the
  coach can answer usefully.
- Ratings, reports and block lists.

3.4 Device, session and technical data

Collected automatically each time you sign in or use the app:

- Device model, operating system and version, and whether the device is
  physical or an emulator
- A device identifier used to distinguish your sessions
- IP address, and the approximate country and city derived from it via
  the third-party lookup service freegeoip.app. Feeziq does not request
  or use GPS or precise device location.
- Login and last-active timestamps
- Firebase Cloud Messaging push tokens
- App version, language and locale
- Crash and diagnostic information

You can view every active session and sign a device out remotely from
Settings, under Sessions.

3.5 Usage and analytics data

Through Google Analytics for Firebase we collect screens viewed,
features used, AI features invoked, workouts started and completed,
subscription and purchase events, and your user ID so events can be
attributed to your account. When you sign out we stop attributing events
to you.

3.6 Advertising data

If you are on a free plan, Google AdMob serves banner and rewarded ads
and may collect device identifiers, advertising identifiers, IP address
and ad interaction data. On iOS, Feeziq does not present the App
Tracking Transparency prompt and does not request permission to track
you across apps, so no cross-app tracking identifier is made available
to advertisers through us. Ads are removed entirely on a paid
subscription.

3.7 Purchase data

Subscriptions are sold through the Apple App Store and Google Play and
managed by RevenueCat. RevenueCat receives your Feeziq user ID, purchase
receipts, entitlement status, product and transaction identifiers, and
device platform. We never receive or store your card number, bank
details or billing address. Those stay with Apple and Google.

3.8 What we do not collect

- Precise or background location
- Contacts, calendar, SMS or call logs
- HealthKit or Google Fit data
- Audio recordings. The microphone permission string that ships in the
  iOS app exists only because the system media picker declares it.
  Feeziq records no audio.
- Biometric identifiers, government IDs, or payment card data


4. HOW WE USE YOUR DATA, AND ON WHAT LEGAL BASIS

- To provide the app (accounts, workouts, diets, tracking, messaging and
  social features): performance of our contract with you, GDPR Article
  6(1)(b).
- To process your health and fitness entries: your explicit consent,
  Article 9(2)(a).
- To generate AI workouts, diets, food and activity recognition, and AI
  Coach answers: contract, plus explicit consent for the health inputs.
- To send push notifications you have enabled (reminders, messages,
  social activity): contract, or consent where the device requires it.
- For session security, device management, fraud and abuse prevention,
  and App Check attestation: our legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f).
- To measure and improve the app through analytics: legitimate
  interests, or consent where required.
- To serve advertising to free accounts: consent where required,
  otherwise legitimate interests.
- To bill and manage subscriptions: contract.
- To meet legal, tax and app-store obligations: legal obligation,
  Article 6(1)(c).

We do not make decisions with legal or similarly significant effects
about you using solely automated processing. AI-generated plans are
suggestions, not decisions about your rights.


5. AI FEATURES IN DETAIL

Feeziq uses Google Vertex AI (Gemini models) through Firebase AI Logic
for:

- Meal photo scanning. The photo you take or choose is sent to Gemini
  for nutritional estimation.
- Meal and activity descriptions. The text you type is sent to Gemini.
- Workout and diet plan generation. Your fitness profile (age, gender,
  height, weight, activity level, goal, sports and dietary
  restrictions) is sent to Gemini.
- AI Coach. Your messages, plus a summary of your fitness profile, are
  sent to Gemini for each conversation.

What you should know:

1. Google acts as our processor for these calls. Under the Google Cloud
   and Vertex AI terms that apply to Feeziq, your prompts and responses
   are not used to train Google's models.
2. AI output is an estimate. Calorie counts, macros and plans are
   approximations and are frequently wrong in detail.
3. Do not type medical details, diagnoses, medication or anything else
   you would not want processed by a third-party AI service into
   free-text AI fields. Send only what the feature needs.
4. AI conversations and generated plans you save are stored with your
   account and are deleted when you delete your account.


6. WHO WE SHARE DATA WITH

We do not sell your data and we do not share it for cross-context
behavioural advertising. We use the following service providers, each
bound to process data on our instructions:

- Google Firebase (Authentication, Firestore, Realtime Database, Cloud
  Storage, Cloud Functions, Cloud Messaging, App Check and Analytics)
  receives substantially all account, health, content and device data.
  This is our backend. Role: processor.
- Google Vertex AI receives AI prompts: meal photos, descriptions,
  fitness profile and coach messages. Role: processor.
- Google AdMob receives device and advertising identifiers, IP address
  and ad interactions. It receives no health data. Role: independent or
  joint controller, depending on jurisdiction.
- RevenueCat receives your user ID, purchase receipts, entitlement and
  transaction data. Role: processor.
- Apple App Store and Google Play receive purchase and subscription
  data. Role: independent controllers.
- Open Food Facts receives the barcode number you scan, and nothing
  else. No account data, no health data, no photo. Role: independent
  controller of an open database.
- freegeoip.app receives your IP address in order to return an
  approximate country and city. Role: processor.

We also disclose data where legally required, such as under a court
order or lawful request; to establish or defend legal claims; to protect
the safety of users; and, with notice to you, to a successor entity if
Feeziq is ever sold or merged.


7. WHAT OTHER USERS CAN SEE

Feeziq is social. By design, other users can see:

- Your username, display name, profile photo and biography
- Your sports, XP, streak, achievements, and follower and following
  counts
- Your position on public and monthly leaderboards
- Your presence indicator inside a chat you share with them
- Your messages, visible to the person you send them to
- Aggregated, non-identifying contributions to the community activity
  feed and global statistics

Other users cannot see your email address, date of birth, weight, meals,
hydration, body metrics, sessions or device information.

You can block a user at any time, which stops messages in both
directions.


8. HOW LONG WE KEEP DATA

- Account and health data: kept while your account exists.
- After account deletion: removed from live systems promptly, and purged
  from encrypted backups within 90 days.
- Messages: deleted with the account. A message you sent remains visible
  in the recipient's copy of the conversation until they delete it.
- Session records: retained while the session is active. Revoked
  sessions are deleted.
- Analytics: retained by Google Analytics for Firebase for a maximum of
  14 months.
- Transaction and tax records: retained as long as tax and accounting
  law requires, typically seven years, independently of account
  deletion.


9. SECURITY

- All traffic between the app and our backend uses TLS.
- Authentication is handled by Firebase Authentication. We never hold
  your plaintext password.
- Direct-message content is AES-encrypted before it is written to the
  database and to local storage. The encryption key is held in the
  platform keystore, the iOS Keychain or the Android Keystore, rather
  than in app code.
- Requests are attested with Firebase App Check to reduce abuse of our
  backend from unauthorised clients.
- Access to production data is limited to the operator of Feeziq.

No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal data
and creates a risk to you, we will notify you and the relevant
supervisory authority as required by law, within 72 hours of becoming
aware under GDPR.


10. INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS

Feeziq runs on Google Cloud and Firebase. Your data is processed on
Google infrastructure that may be located in the United States and other
countries outside your own. For transfers out of the EEA, the UK or
Switzerland we rely on the European Commission's Standard Contractual
Clauses and the UK Addendum, incorporated into our agreements with
Google and our other processors, together with the safeguards those
providers apply.


11. YOUR RIGHTS

Wherever you live, you may ask us to:

- Give you access to the personal data we hold about you, and a copy of
  it
- Correct anything inaccurate. Most profile and health fields are
  editable in the app.
- Delete your account and data
- Export your data in a portable, machine-readable format
- Restrict or stop processing based on legitimate interests
- Honour the withdrawal of your consent at any time, including consent
  to health-data processing

You will not be treated differently for exercising any of these rights.

How to exercise them: delete your account yourself at feeziq.com, which
is where Settings, then Account, then Delete Account will take you, or
contact us through feeziq.com. We respond within 30 days, extendable by
a further 60 days for complex requests, and we will tell you if we need
more time. We may ask you to verify control of your account email before
acting on a request.

If you are in California

Under the CCPA and CPRA you have the rights above, plus the right to
know the categories of personal information we collect, the sources, the
business purpose, and the categories of third parties involved. These
are set out in sections 3 and 6.

We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for
cross-context behavioural advertising. Feeziq does not request App
Tracking Transparency permission on iOS. The health and fitness
information you enter is sensitive personal information under the CPRA.
We use it only to provide the service you asked for, and for no
secondary purpose that would trigger a right to limit its use.

If you are in the EEA or the UK

You additionally have the right to lodge a complaint with your
supervisory authority. In the UK this is the Information Commissioner's
Office, at ico.org.uk.


12. CHILDREN

Feeziq is not intended for children under 16 in the EEA and the UK, or
under 13 elsewhere, and we do not knowingly collect data from them. If
you believe a child has created an account, contact us through
feeziq.com and we will delete it. Where a higher local age of digital
consent applies, that age applies to you.


13. NOT MEDICAL ADVICE

Feeziq is a fitness and wellness tool. It is not a medical device and
not a healthcare provider. Its plans, calorie estimates and AI Coach
responses are informational only, and are not a diagnosis, a treatment
or professional advice. Talk to a qualified clinician before starting a
new exercise or diet programme, particularly if you are pregnant, have a
medical condition, or take medication.


14. PUSH NOTIFICATIONS AND EMAIL

You can turn off push notifications in your device settings or in
Feeziq's notification settings at any time. We will still send essential
service emails, such as security alerts and account and billing notices,
because these are part of operating your account.


15. THIRD-PARTY LINKS

The app links out to feeziq.com, our terms of use, app store pages and
occasional external resources. Those destinations have their own privacy
policies, and this one does not cover them.


16. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY

We will update this policy as Feeziq changes. The "Last updated" date at
the top always reflects the current version. For material changes, such
as a new category of data, a new purpose or a new class of recipient, we
will notify you in the app or by email before the change takes effect,
and where the law requires it we will ask for your consent again.


